          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.332,
            0.585,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": "Is –17 one more or one less than –16?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.629,
            0.311,
            0.842,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.391,
            0.292,
            0.414
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.417,
            0.847,
            0.455
          ],
          "content": "1. Fill in the blanks with numbers, and boxes with operation signs such that the expressions on both sides are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.459,
            0.519,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "(a) $24+(6-4)=24+6$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.483,
            0.567,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": "(b) $38+(\\boxed{\\quad}\\boxed{\\quad}\\boxed{\\quad}=38+9-4$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.507,
            0.493,
            0.527
          ],
          "content": "(c) $24-(6+4)=24$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.532,
            0.514,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": "(d) 24 – 6 – 4 = 24 – 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.556,
            0.456,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": "(e) $27-(8+3)=27\\ 8\\ 3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.579,
            0.561,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": "(f) $27-(27-8+3)=27-8+3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.605,
            0.846,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": "2. Remove the brackets and write the expression having the same value."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.647,
            0.388,
            0.666
          ],
          "content": "(a) $1 4 \\pm ( 1 2 \\pm 1 0 )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.647,
            0.724,
            0.666
          ],
          "content": "(b) $1 4 - ( 1 2 \\pm 1 0 )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.671,
            0.387,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": "(c) $1 4 \\pm ( 1 2 - 1 0 )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.671,
            0.723,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": "(d) $1 4 - ( 1 2 - 1 0 )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.695,
            0.396,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": "(e) $-14+(12-10)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.695,
            0.733,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": "(f) $1 4 - ( - 1 2 - 1 0 )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.719,
            0.848,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": "3. \tFind the values of the following expressions. For each pair, first try to guess whether they have the same value. When are the two expressions equal?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.78,
            0.517,
            0.799
          ],
          "content": "(a) (6 + 10) – 2 and 6 + (10 – 2)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.804,
            0.516,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": "(b) 16 – (8 – 3) and (16 – 8) – 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.829,
            0.55,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": "(c) 27 – (18 + 4) and 27 + (–18 – 4)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.853,
            0.848,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": "4. In each of the sets of expressions below, identify those that have the same value. Do not evaluate them, but rather use your understanding of terms."
        },
